<BaseLayout title="Emergency Support">
  <h1>Emergency Support</h1>

  <p>
    If you are in immediate danger or feel unable to keep yourself safe, please
    contact emergency services or a crisis line in your region. Identity
    Partners cannot provide crisis intervention or emergency response.
  </p>

  <h2>United Kingdom</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>999</strong> — Emergency services (police, fire, ambulance)</li>
    <li><strong>111</strong> — NHS urgent medical help</li>
    <li><strong>Samaritans</strong> — 116 123 (24/7 listening support)</li>
    <li><strong>Shout</strong> — Text <em>SHOUT</em> to 85258</li>
    <li><strong>BEAT Eating Disorders</strong> — 0808 801 0677</li>
    <li><strong>Mind</strong> — 0300 123 3393</li>
    <li><strong>Refuge</strong> — 0808 2000 247 (domestic abuse)</li>
    <li><strong>Childline</strong> — 0800 1111 (under 18s)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Australia</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>000</strong> — Emergency services</li>
    <li><strong>Lifeline</strong> — 13 11 14</li>
    <li><strong>Beyond Blue</strong> — 1300 22 4636</li>
    <li><strong>Kids Helpline</strong> — 1800 55 1800</li>
    <li><strong>Suicide Call Back Service</strong> — 1300 659 467</li>
    <li><strong>Domestic Violence Line</strong> — 1800 737 732</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>New Zealand</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>111</strong> — Emergency services</li>
    <li><strong>Lifeline NZ</strong> — 0800 543 354</li>
    <li><strong>Youthline</strong> — 0800 376 633</li>
    <li><strong>Depression Helpline</strong> — 0800 111 757</li>
    <li><strong>Safe to Talk</strong> — 0800 044 334</li>
    <li><strong>What’s Up</strong> — 0800 942 8787 (children & teens)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>North America</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>911</strong> — Emergency services</li>
    <li><strong>988 Suicide & Crisis Lifeline</strong> — Call or text 988</li>
    <li><strong>Crisis Text Line</strong> — Text <em>HOME</em> to 741741</li>
    <li><strong>NEDA</strong> — Eating disorders support</li>
    <li><strong>SAMHSA</strong> — 1-800-662-HELP (substance use & mental health)</li>
    <li><strong>Trevor Project</strong> — 1-866-488-7386 (LGBTQ+ youth)</li>
    <li><strong>National Domestic Violence Hotline</strong> — 1-800-799-7233</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    If none of these services feel right, please reach out to any trusted person
    or local support organisation. You do not need to navigate crisis alone.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
